References: <OF9485C0C6.688B8FF3-ON882570AE.006A0617-882570AE.006A4F1A@biogenidec.com>
Message-ID: <436F5D24.5090902@med.umich.edu>

Daniel Pick wrote:
> Hello,
>     I would like to apply gcrma to a custom chip for which I have the probe
> sequence information.  gcrma appears to automatically go to the Internet to
> search for the appropriate probe package.  How do I override this behavior
> to look for a ProbePackage built and installed locally?

Did you give the probe package a name, or did you accept the default 
one? If you didn't give the probe package the expected name, gcrma() is 
not going to be able to find it. If you passed a name to 
makeProbePackage(), your best bet is to uninstall the existing package, 
and re-make the probe package without passing a name. This will give it 
the default name, which gcrma() will then be able to find.

HTH,

Jim


