A note on installation - it is a common misperception that a package can be simply zipped up and then installed using e.g., the pulldown menu in Rgui. This actually was the case back in the day for non-source code containing packages (maybe < R-1.6.0 or so?), but no longer. In order to install these packages, you have to use R CMD INSTALL at a command prompt. 

On Unix and Linux this is straightforward because these OSes usually come with all the required software. However, on Windows, you need to install some extra software and get it configured correctly. Instructions on how to do this can be found in section 5.1 and Appendix F of 'R Installation and Administration'. It can be a life saver to be able to install source packages on Windows, so for many users it is worth the pain to get set up.

