From bmb at bmbolstad.com  Wed Nov 23 17:19:16 2005
From: bmb at bmbolstad.com (Ben Bolstad)
Date: Wed, 23 Nov 2005 08:19:16 -0800
Subject: [BioC] How to save jpegs of all MAplots of an affybatch
In-Reply-To: <BAY108-F9B9C71F7231C7321C1B9CC6550@phx.gbl>
References: <BAY108-F9B9C71F7231C7321C1B9CC6550@phx.gbl>
Message-ID: <1132762756.3198.5.camel@localhost.localdomain>

The easiest way is something like

jpeg("MAplot%03d.jpeg")
MAplot(mysamples)
dev.off()

which would write files MAplot001.jpeg, MAplot002.jpeg, ......



Alternatively, you could use the ref argument to MAplot (to make one of
the arrays the reference) and generate n-1 MAplots using your loop
structure. eg

for(i in 2:n){
jpeg(file=paste(sampleNames(mysamples[,i]),"MAplot.jpeg", sep=""))
MAplot(mysamples[,i],ref=1)
dev.off()



